@dossier_public_ledger
title: Put every milestone, ministry and deadline on one public ledger
subtitle: Every cabinet party signs a dated column, including ours. The ledger stays readable until August 2026.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones += 4;
Q.kpo_delivery += 2;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 3);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 2;
Q.public_trust += 3;
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.psl_relation += 1;
Q.razem_dissent -= 3;
Q.kpo_ledger_public = 1;
Q.kpo_owner = "shared";
Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "A dated public ledger carries every cabinet party's column, ours included";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 2;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 2;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "A common public ledger makes later credit claims auditable.";
Q.news_headline = "The coalition publishes a ministry-by-ministry KPO ledger";
!}

Every milestone goes onto one page: the line, the ministry answerable for it,
the date it is due. Nothing about the document is generous. A minister who
misses a deadline misses it in public, printed directly beneath a line somebody
else in the same cabinet delivered on time.

**[+ kpo_partner_leader +]** signs because refusing to sign is the only version
of this week that makes the evening news. [+ kpo_partner_name +] understands
what it has agreed to by the second Tuesday, when a journalist telephones a
named deputy minister about one housing line rather than telephoning the
Chancellery about the fund in general.

So do we. Our own columns are on the same page, in the same typeface, and
**[+ razem_leader +]** observes that Lewica has just published the evidence for
its own prosecution eighteen months early. That is the trade: the instrument
that will hold a partner to a date in 2025 is the instrument that will hold us
to one.

- @kpo_result: File the ledger

@dossier_left_earmarks
title: Reserve the Left's claim for housing, care and local services
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Lewica's name goes on the social annexes, and [+ kpo_partner_name +] is told which lines it has lost.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party cannot staff a parallel investment team.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
Q.kpo_delivery += 4;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 5;
if (Q.kpo_partner_code == "ko") {
    Q.ko_relation -= 4;
    Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 3;
} else if (Q.kpo_partner_code == "p2050") {
    Q.p2050_relation -= 4;
    Q.p2050_coalition_dissent += 3;
} else if (Q.kpo_partner_code == "psl") {
    Q.psl_relation -= 4;
    Q.psl_coalition_dissent += 3;
} else if (Q.kpo_partner_code == "pis") {
    Q.pis_relation -= 4;
} else {
    Q.ko_relation -= 3;
    Q.psl_relation -= 1;
}
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 2;
Q.labor_credibility += 3;
Q.local_network += 2;
Q.kpo_owner = "lewica";
Q.kpo_owner_label = "Lewica's name is on the social annexes and nobody else's";
Q.kpo_grudge_active = 1;
Q.kpo_grudge_code = Q.kpo_partner_code;
Q.kpo_grudge_name = Q.kpo_partner_name;
Q.kpo_grudge_leader = Q.kpo_partner_leader;
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = "the February 2024 raid on the social annexes";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 5;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 4;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The Left attaches its name to a concrete social-investment file.";
Q.news_headline = "Lewica marks housing, care and local services as its KPO share";
!}

Our own people spend four days inside the annexes and come back with the lines
that photograph: social housing, care places, the bus routes that stopped
running in 2019 and were never restored. Those become the Lewica file — staffed
by Lewica officials, costed by Lewica economists, defended in committee under
our name and nobody else's.

**[+ kpo_partner_leader +]** calls it a raid on a common fund, in those words,
to a camera. It is a raid on a common fund. The calculation is simply that a
fund with no author is remembered as the government's, and a government is a
thing voters can already name without any help from us.

[+ kpo_partner_name +] does not forget it. Somewhere in the next two years there
will be a vote we need, a ministry we have to persuade or a budget line we have
to ask for, and the person on the other side of the table will have been in the
room this afternoon.

- @kpo_result: Claim the social file

@dossier_fast_claim
title: File quickly behind Prime Minister [+ prime_minister +]
subtitle: A fortnight of queue position, bought with the Chancellery's signature rather than a shared one.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones += 3;
Q.kpo_delivery += 1;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 2);
const leftOwnsPremiership = Q.government_party == "lewica";
Q.kpo_owner = leftOwnsPremiership ? "lewica" : "chancellery";
Q.kpo_owner_label = leftOwnsPremiership
    ? "Lewica's own Chancellery signed the claim and owns it"
    : Q.prime_minister + "'s Chancellery signed the claim alone";
if (leftOwnsPremiership) {
    Q.kpo_public_credit += 3;
    Q.government_delivery += 2;
    Q.party_unity += 2;
    Q.razem_dissent -= 2;
    Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 2;
    Q.psl_coalition_dissent += 1;
    Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 3;
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "The file moves faster, and Lewica's prime minister owns the result.";
} else {
    Q.kpo_public_credit -= 2;
    if (Q.government_party == "ko") {
        Q.ko_relation += 4;
        Q.ko_coalition_dissent -= 2;
    } else if (Q.government_party == "psl") {
        Q.psl_relation += 4;
        Q.psl_coalition_dissent -= 2;
    } else if (Q.government_party == "p2050") {
        Q.p2050_relation += 4;
        Q.p2050_coalition_dissent -= 2;
    } else {
        Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 2;
    }
    Q.razem_dissent += 4;
    Q.kpo_last_credit_change = -2;
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "The file moves faster, but the Left disappears behind " +
        Q.prime_minister + ".";
}
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 1;
Q.news_headline = Q.prime_minister + " submits a rapid common KPO claim";
!}

The claim goes to Brussels inside a fortnight, unamended, with the Chancellery's
covering letter on top of it. Speed is worth something real and unglamorous: the
Commission's desk officers are working a queue, and a file that arrives early
and tidy is a file that gets read in March instead of June.

[? if government_party = "lewica": The letter is signed by our own prime minister, so the tidiness and the queue position both belong to us. **[+ razem_leader +]** notes, without much warmth, that the quickest way to look like a party of government is to behave like one, and that this is not a compliment. **[+ kpo_partner_leader +]** wanted two more weeks and an amendment; [+ kpo_partner_name +] has been told it can have the amendment in the next request.?]
[? if government_party != "lewica": **[+ prime_minister +]** announces it alone from the Chancellery steps, because the letter went out under the Chancellery's name and nobody in our delegation thought to ask for a second signature on it. The signature was the only thing on offer that we could have kept.?]
[? if government_party != "lewica": **[+ razem_leader +]** asks what exactly we bought with the fortnight. The honest answer is a queue position in Brussels that will be invisible to every voter in Poland and will still, in April, be the reason the money arrives at all.?]

- @kpo_result: Send the rapid claim

@dossier_opposition_audit
title: Stand up a permanent social-investment and milestone audit
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Three staff and a standing brief — the team survives into the 2025 contract fights.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Opposition scrutiny needs staff, data work and legal capacity.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 2;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 3;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.labor_credibility += 2;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 2;
Q.kpo_opposition_file = 1;
Q.kpo_owner = "none";
Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "The file belongs to the cabinet; Lewica keeps a standing audit team on it";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 3;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "Opposition scrutiny wins credit without pretending to control the payment.";
Q.news_headline = "The Left publishes the missing social side of the KPO ledger";
!}

Two researchers and a lawyer spend the month inside annexes nobody in the press
gallery has opened. What they publish is not an accusation but a comparison: the
milestones the plan promises against the housing, care and local lines that went
missing somewhere between the draft and the submission, with the date each one
disappeared.

**[+ prime_minister +]**'s government is not obliged to answer an opposition
document, and does not. It is obliged to answer the mayors who read it and
recognised their own withdrawn projects in the second table, and three of them
say so on regional television inside a week.

The audit's real value is that it does not end. Three people now hold a
standing brief on this fund, and they will still be holding it when the
contracts start being signed — which is the point at which a monitoring team is
worth ten press conferences.

- @kpo_result: Publish the audit

@dossier_opposition_record
title: Table written questions and record the missing milestones
subtitle: Always available in opposition. A numbered paper trail, no staff, and nothing that survives past the answer deadline.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 1;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 1;
Q.kpo_owner = "none";
Q.kpo_owner_label = "The file belongs to the cabinet and Lewica watches it from the chamber";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 1;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "Written questions preserve an opposition record without claiming to complete a milestone audit.";
Q.news_headline = "Lewica records the missing KPO milestones in Parliament";
!}

The questions go in under parliamentary rules: numbered, dated, requiring a
signed answer within thirty days. It costs the club one morning and produces no
headline whatsoever. Nobody outside the chamber notices, including the ministry,
which answers three of the seven properly.

What it produces is a record. When a minister stands up in 2026 and says the
social lines were never in the plan, there will be a signed reply on file saying
something else, over that minister's own name.

It is the cheapest instrument available to us and the slowest, and it builds
nothing. Next year, when the contracts are being signed and somebody needs to
read four thousand of them, we will still have nobody whose job that is.

- @kpo_result: File the questions


@kpo_first_payment_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — Authorised payment and repaired courts stay properly distinct, the €6.3 billion arrives into a named argument between the Chancellery, the finance ministry and the party that signed February's file, and each of the six routes lands somewhere concrete: open calls, ribbon-cutting flagships, an invisible co-financing reserve, a published correction file.
title: The first KPO payment
subtitle: €6.3 billion lands, and the coalition has ten days to decide who it belongs to.
face-image: img/poland/events/kpo.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
