@payment_social_capacity
title: Open transparent calls for housing, care and local transport
subtitle: Spends two released tranches on local capacity Lewica can point at.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and kpo_first_payment_paid = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_funds_spent += 2;
Q.kpo_delivery += 5;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 4;
Q.government_delivery += 4;
Q.local_network += 3;
Q.public_trust += 3;
Q.psl_relation += 2;
Q.kpo_owner = "lewica";
Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "Lewica's ministry wrote the open calls and will answer for the scoring";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change += 4;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 5;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "Open calls turn the first transfer into visible local capacity.";
Q.news_headline = "The first KPO calls fund care, housing and local links";
!}

The calls go out unrestricted. Any municipality with a site and a signature can
bid, the scoring sheet is published alongside the call, and the deadline is the
same for a city of eight hundred thousand and a gmina of four. Housing
associations, care providers and two dozen county transport authorities discover
that they are allowed to want something.

**[+ economy_minister +]**'s officials argue against open competition for three
days, in writing, and their argument is not corrupt: open calls produce winners
nobody in the ministry chose, on timetables nobody in the ministry set, and the
department will be answerable for all of them. That is precisely the point.

Hajnówka bids for a bus contract it has been unable to fund since 2019. So do
forty other places that have never once been the named beneficiary of a national
programme, and roughly half of them will be turned down — this time with a
published score beside their name instead of a silence.

- @kpo_result: Open the first calls

@payment_prime_minister
title: Concentrate the first tranche in government flagships
subtitle: Spends three released tranches on schemes big enough to be opened with a ribbon, and small enough in number to be opened by one person.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and kpo_first_payment_paid = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_funds_spent += 3;
Q.kpo_delivery += 4;
Q.government_delivery += 5;
Q.kpo_owner = Q.government_party == "lewica" ? "lewica" : "chancellery";
Q.kpo_owner_label = Q.government_party == "lewica"
    ? "Lewica's Chancellery picked the flagships and owns every one of them"
    : Q.prime_minister + "'s Chancellery owns the flagships and the photographs";
if (Q.government_party == "lewica") {
    Q.kpo_public_credit += 3;
    Q.party_unity += 2;
    Q.razem_dissent -= 1;
    Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 2;
    Q.psl_coalition_dissent += 1;
    Q.kpo_last_credit_change += 3;
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "Flagship projects move, and Lewica's Chancellery owns the credit and the risk.";
} else {
    Q.kpo_public_credit -= 3;
    if (Q.government_party == "ko") {
        Q.ko_relation += 4;
        Q.ko_coalition_dissent -= 3;
    } else if (Q.government_party == "psl") {
        Q.psl_relation += 4;
        Q.psl_coalition_dissent -= 3;
    } else if (Q.government_party == "p2050") {
        Q.p2050_relation += 4;
        Q.p2050_coalition_dissent -= 3;
    } else {
        Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 3;
    }
    Q.barons_dissent += 2;
    Q.progressives_dissent += 3;
    Q.kpo_last_credit_change -= 3;
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "Flagship projects move, while coalition credit centralises around " +
        Q.prime_minister + ".";
}
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 4;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.prime_minister + " concentrates the first recovery projects";
!}

The money goes into eleven large schemes, each of which can be opened by a
minister holding scissors. They are real projects, they will be finished, and
they were selected for the size of the hoarding rather than for the state of the
bus timetable in the county they sit in. Hajnówka is not on the list. Hajnówka
was never going to be on this kind of list.

[? if government_party = "lewica": Our own Chancellery took the decision, which spares us a coalition argument and hands us every word of the criticism. **[+ kpo_partner_leader +]** is generous in public and privately delighted: [+ kpo_partner_name +] gets three of the eleven ribbons without having had to defend the selection to anybody.?]
[? if government_party != "lewica": **[+ prime_minister +]** takes the podium at the first opening. Lewica's ministers are in the second row of the photograph, having supplied the votes that made the fund available and the officials who wrote two of the eleven files.?]
[? if government_party != "lewica" and kpo_prior_owner = "lewica": The February annexes carried our name. This photograph does not, and by June the two facts will have merged in the public record into a single government achievement.?]

- @kpo_result: Concentrate the tranche

@payment_cofinance
title: Hold a co-financing reserve for the year-end budget
subtitle: Holds one released tranche against December's co-financing; nothing visible this year.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and kpo_first_payment_paid = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_funds_spent += 1;
Q.budget += 2;
Q.kpo_delivery += 1;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 1;
Q.fiscal_stress = Math.max(0, Q.fiscal_stress - 2);
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.kpo_grudge_active = 0;
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = "";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change += 1;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 1;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "A reserve creates budget capacity, though few voters can see it yet.";
Q.news_headline = "KPO co-financing gives the coalition room before the budget";
!}

The tranche is not spent. It is parked against the co-financing the December
budget will need, where it will prevent, quietly and in advance, a fight about
the deficit that would otherwise be settled by removing a social line.

**[+ finance_minister +]** is the only person in the building who fully
understands what has just been handed over, and behaves accordingly. Whatever we
have taken from this coalition since February is now, in the ministry's ledger,
paid back with interest — and a finance minister who owes you a favour is worth
more in December than a ribbon is worth in April.

It is the most useful thing available and the least visible: no site, no
opening, no photograph, just a number in one spreadsheet that makes next winter
survivable. Our organisers ask, reasonably, what they are supposed to say at the
door.

- @kpo_result: Hold the reserve

@payment_correction
title: Concede the defects and publish a sixty-day correction file
subtitle: Name the weak annexes, name who signed them, and make [+ kpo_partner_name +] stand next to the admission.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and kpo_first_payment_paid = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones += 4;
Q.kpo_delivery += 2;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 4);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 1;
Q.government_procedural_restraint += 3;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 2;
Q.kpo_owner = "shared";
Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "Every cabinet party signed the correction file, so every one of them owns the defects";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 1;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 2;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "Owning the delay limits the panic and creates a credible correction route.";
Q.news_headline = "The government publishes the defects in its own KPO file";
!}

We put the defects in writing before the Commission's second letter can force
us to: which annexes were weak, which official signed each one off, and the
sixty days inside which each will be repaired. It is a deeply unpleasant
document to publish under your own government's masthead, and the first draft
comes back from three ministries with the names removed.

The names go back in. That is the entire value of the exercise — a file that
admits its faults on a published schedule is a file Brussels can keep working
with, and one that admits them anonymously is a press release.

**[+ kpo_partner_leader +]** signs at the second meeting, after establishing
that [+ kpo_partner_name +] drafted four of the weak annexes and that this fact
is already in the document. Nobody is carrying this one alone, which is the
nearest thing to solidarity a coalition produces in a bad month.

- @kpo_result: Publish the correction file

@payment_opposition_dashboard
title: Track contracts, milestones and beneficiaries outside government
subtitle: [? if kpo_opposition_file = 1: February's audit team already has the data pipeline; the dashboard costs nothing further.?][? if kpo_opposition_file = 0: Cost: 1 resource to build the contracts database from nothing.?]
view-if: left_in_government = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1 or kpo_opposition_file = 1
unavailable-subtitle: With no standing audit team, the opposition cannot fund the contracts database.
on-arrival: {!
// February's standing audit team is the difference between extending a data
// pipeline and building one; without it the dashboard costs a resource.
const dashboardTeamExists = Q.kpo_opposition_file ? 1 : 0;
if (!dashboardTeamExists) Q.resources -= 1;
Q.kpo_public_credit += dashboardTeamExists ? 4 : 3;
Q.media_capacity += 3;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.local_network += 2;
Q.kpo_scrutiny += dashboardTeamExists ? 2 : 1;
Q.kpo_opposition_file = 1;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change += dashboardTeamExists ? 4 : 3;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The Left cannot allocate the transfer, but it can make ownership harder to fake.";
Q.news_headline = "An opposition KPO dashboard follows every contract";
!}

Contracts, beneficiaries and milestone dates go onto a public page that updates
whenever the government publishes anything at all. It is unglamorous work: two
staff, a spreadsheet with fourteen thousand rows, and an inexhaustible patience
with procurement portals that time out at four in the afternoon.

[? if kpo_opposition_file = 1: February's audit team already knew where the data lived, which is the whole difference between a launch and a rebuild. They had the beneficiary map scraped before the ministry published its own version of it.?]
[? if kpo_opposition_file = 0: Everything is built from nothing, in eight weeks, by people who had other jobs in March. Half the delay is spent discovering which of the ministry's three registers is the one that is actually maintained.?]

Journalists start using it inside a month, because nothing else assembles the
same information in one place, and **[+ prime_minister +]**'s press office
begins pre-empting the awkward rows before we publish them. We cannot direct a
złoty of this money. We can make it very much harder for anybody to stand in
front of a project that has not started.

- @kpo_result: Open the dashboard

@payment_opposition_record
title: Request the public contracts register and record unanswered questions
subtitle: Always available in opposition. Existing disclosures only — no team, no database, no capacity that outlives the month.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 1;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 1;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change += 1;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "A basic parliamentary record exposes unanswered contract questions without pretending to monitor every beneficiary.";
Q.news_headline = "Lewica files a basic public record of the first KPO contracts";
!}

We request the contracts register through the ordinary disclosure route and log
every question the ministry declines to answer. There is no dashboard, no staff
and no launch — only a numbered paper trail and, eventually, a partial reply
citing commercial confidentiality over eleven of the entries.

It is the version of scrutiny available to a party that cannot fund a monitoring
team. Thin, but a thin record still contradicts a confident minister eighteen
months from now, and eighteen months from now is exactly when this fund becomes
interesting to everybody else.

- @kpo_result: File the register request


@kpo_article7_credit_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — Closure is never confused with repair, the surviving-PiS fork gives the frozen file a competence argument rather than a sovereignty one, February's ledger decides whether a shared scoreboard can exist at all, and all six responses name who banks the credit and what it will be spent on in December.
title: Who owns European normalisation?
subtitle: Six years of Article 7 close in an afternoon, and the coalition spends the evening arguing about a photograph.
face-image: img/poland/events/kpo.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 20
order: 20
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 5
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 0;
Q.kpo_article7_reward = Q.government_party != "pis" ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_funds_available =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_available))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_funds_available)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_funds_spent =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_spent))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_funds_spent)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_public_credit =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_public_credit))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_public_credit)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_delivery =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_delivery)) ? Number(Q.kpo_delivery) : 0;
Q.kpo_milestones =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_milestones))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_milestones)
        : 0;
const kpoNames24c = {
    ko: "KO",
    p2050: "Poland 2050",
    psl: "PSL",
    pis: "PiS",
    konf: "Konfederacja"
};
const kpoSeats24c = function(code) {
    return Q["ministry_" + code + "_in_cabinet"]
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q[code + "_seats"]) || 0)
        : 0;
};
Q.kpo_partner_code = Object.keys(kpoNames24c)
    .filter(function(code) { return kpoSeats24c(code) > 0; })
    .sort(function(first, second) {
        return (second == Q.government_party ? 1e6 : kpoSeats24c(second)) -
            (first == Q.government_party ? 1e6 : kpoSeats24c(first));
    })[0] || "";
Q.kpo_partner_name =
    kpoNames24c[Q.kpo_partner_code] || "the coalition's other parties";
Q.kpo_partner_leader =
    String(Q[Q.kpo_partner_code + "_leader"] || "").trim() ||
    String(Q.prime_minister || "the senior partner");
Q.kpo_ledger_public = Q.kpo_ledger_public ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_prior_ledger = Q.kpo_ledger_public;
Q.kpo_opposition_file = Q.kpo_opposition_file ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_owner = String(Q.kpo_owner || "none");
Q.kpo_prior_owner = Q.kpo_owner;
Q.kpo_grudge_active = Q.kpo_grudge_active ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_grudge_name = String(Q.kpo_grudge_name || "");
Q.kpo_grudge_leader = String(Q.kpo_grudge_leader || "");
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = String(Q.kpo_grudge_reason || "");
Q.kpo_uncommitted = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.kpo_funds_available - Q.kpo_funds_spent
);
if (Q.kpo_article7_reward) {
    Q.rule_of_law_eu_status = "Article 7 closed; domestic repair monitored";
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "European confidence improves before the domestic legal conflict is finished.";
    Q.news_headline =
        "Article 7 closes and the coalition opens a credit war";
} else {
    Q.rule_of_law_eu_status =
        "Article 7 remains open under PiS; KPO conditions unmet";
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "The PiS cabinet remains under Article 7 and receives no payment or delivery credit.";
    Q.news_headline =
        "Article 7 and the recovery-fund file remain stalled under PiS";
}
!}

= May 2024 — Europe judges the legal record

[? if kpo_article7_reward: The Council closes the Article 7 procedure. It has been open against Poland since December 2017; it closes in an afternoon, in a room in Brussels, with a short statement and no ceremony. That is a diplomatic and fiscal reward for a changed political situation. It is not a certificate that any particular Polish court, prosecutor or appointment has been put right, and the people who will have to live with the ones that have not are not in the room either.?]
[? if not kpo_article7_reward: The surviving PiS cabinet has supplied neither the political change nor the legal milestones that closure requires. Article 7 stays open, the payment stays unavailable, and **[+ pis_leader +]** describes the procedure to a party congress as proof that Poland is being punished for existing. Lewica can document the failure precisely. Lewica cannot manufacture European approval from the opposition benches, and should stop implying otherwise.?]

[? if kpo_article7_reward: By the evening the argument has already stopped being about courts. **[+ prime_minister +]** is at the microphone; the question is which parties get to stand behind it, in what order, and whose ministries are named when the money is mentioned in the same sentence.?]
[? if kpo_article7_reward and kpo_public_credit >= 5: Lewica has a recognisable claim on this fund and everybody in the coalition knows it. Which is exactly why [+ kpo_partner_name +] now wants a single government scoreboard with no columns on it.?]
[? if kpo_article7_reward and kpo_public_credit < 5: The government has the European headline and we have supplied votes for it. Nothing yet connects that headline to an object a voter has used, and a headline nobody can touch belongs, by default, to whoever spoke first.?]
[? if kpo_article7_reward and kpo_ledger_public = 1: February's ledger is still the only document in Poland that says which party is answerable for which line, which makes it the only possible basis for an honest scoreboard this week.?]
[? if kpo_article7_reward and kpo_grudge_active: **[+ kpo_grudge_leader +]** has been waiting since February for a week in which [+ kpo_grudge_name +] holds the microphone and we need something. This is that week.?]

- @article7_shared_scoreboard
- @article7_left_delivery
- @article7_pm_credit
- @article7_opposition_truth
- @article7_pis_conditions
- @article7_pis_pressure

@article7_shared_scoreboard
title: Publish one coalition scoreboard and one unresolved-courts annex
subtitle: Requires February's ledger. Every party gets a column; the courts nobody repaired get a page of their own.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and kpo_article7_reward = 1
choose-if: kpo_ledger_public = 1
unavailable-subtitle: No common ledger exists. There is nothing to put columns on, and no agreed record of who owed which line.
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_public_credit += 2;
Q.kpo_delivery += 2;
Q.public_trust += 4;
Q.ko_relation += 3;
Q.psl_relation += 2;
Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 3;
Q.kpo_grudge_active = 0;
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = "";
Q.kpo_owner = "shared";
Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "Credit is divided by column, and the unrepaired courts have a page of their own";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 2;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 2;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "Shared credit buys calm while the annex prevents a false claim of legal completion.";
Q.news_headline = "The coalition separates KPO delivery from unfinished court repair";
!}

February's ledger becomes May's scoreboard: one column per governing party,
each with its delivered lines and its late ones, and behind it an annex that
gets a page to itself — the courts, the prosecutors and the appointments that
Article 7 closure did not touch and was never going to touch.

**[+ kpo_partner_leader +]** would have taken the celebration without the annex
and says so in the meeting, twice. **[+ psl_leader +]** would have preferred
neither document to exist. The scoreboard survives because at this point
refusing to sign it is the only thing that could possibly become the story of
the week, and nobody in the room wants to be that story.

What it buys is calm, which is not nothing: whatever we took from a partner in
February is settled by a document that also credits them. What it costs is the
clean claim. Our lines are in a column beside three other columns, and a column
is not a headline.

- @kpo_result: Publish the scoreboard

@article7_left_delivery
title: Claim the reward through wages, care and public investment
subtitle: [? if kpo_prior_owner = "chancellery": Take the story back off [+ prime_minister +], in public, four weeks after conceding it.?][? if kpo_prior_owner != "chancellery": Put a price in złoty on normalisation and dare [+ kpo_partner_name +] to argue with the figure.?]
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and kpo_article7_reward = 1
on-arrival: {!
// Taking the claim back from a Chancellery we handed it to in February costs
// more inside the coalition and returns less; a claim we never surrendered is
// simply extended.
const reclaimingFromChancellery = Q.kpo_prior_owner == "chancellery" ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_public_credit += reclaimingFromChancellery ? 4 : 6;
Q.kpo_delivery += 3;
Q.labor_credibility += 4;
Q.public_sector_support += 3;
Q.ko_relation -= reclaimingFromChancellery ? 6 : 4;
Q.psl_relation -= 2;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += reclaimingFromChancellery ? 5 : 3;
Q.kpo_owner = "lewica";
Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "Lewica has priced normalisation in wages and care places and signed the invoice";
Q.kpo_grudge_active = 1;
Q.kpo_grudge_code = Q.kpo_partner_code;
Q.kpo_grudge_name = Q.kpo_partner_name;
Q.kpo_grudge_leader = Q.kpo_partner_leader;
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = "the May 2024 social invoice on Article 7 closure";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = reclaimingFromChancellery ? 4 : 6;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 3;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "A clear Left claim travels, and coalition partners immediately contest it.";
Q.news_headline = "Lewica gives European normalisation a social price tag";
!}

We refuse to let normalisation stay a diplomatic abstraction and put a number
next to it: what restored access is worth in wages, in care places, in public
investment — and which of the three we intend to collect first, this year, with
a date.

The claim travels, because it is the only version of this week's news that can
be repeated by somebody who does not know what Article 7 was. It is contested
inside the hour by partners who spent two years grinding through the legal file
and have no intention of watching the Left convert their work into a social
invoice with our letterhead on it.

[? if kpo_prior_owner = "chancellery": Taking it back is worse than never having conceded it. In February we let the Chancellery sign alone; today we are explaining to journalists why the party that stood in the second row is suddenly presenting the bill, and **[+ kpo_partner_leader +]** does not have to say a single word to make that look opportunistic.?]
[? if kpo_prior_owner != "chancellery": **[+ kpo_partner_leader +]** goes on air the same evening to say that the recovery fund is not a Lewica programme. This is entirely true, and it is now the second most repeated sentence of the week, which was the whole objective.?]

- @kpo_result: Attach the price tag

@article7_pm_credit
title: Let [+ prime_minister +] bank the European win for later coalition concessions
subtitle: Hand the whole win to the Chancellery and accept that it will be spent, in December, on somebody's priorities.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and kpo_article7_reward = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_delivery += 1;
Q.kpo_owner = Q.government_party == "lewica" ? "lewica" : "chancellery";
Q.kpo_owner_label = Q.government_party == "lewica"
    ? "Lewica's prime minister banked European normalisation"
    : Q.prime_minister + " banked European normalisation and the leverage with it";
Q.kpo_grudge_active = 0;
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = "";
if (Q.government_party == "lewica") {
    Q.kpo_public_credit += 4;
    Q.government_delivery += 2;
    Q.party_unity += 2;
    Q.razem_dissent -= 1;
    Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 2;
    Q.psl_coalition_dissent += 1;
    Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 4;
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "The cabinet gains stability, and Lewica's prime minister owns the European win.";
} else {
    Q.kpo_public_credit -= 4;
    if (Q.government_party == "ko") {
        Q.ko_relation += 7;
        Q.ko_coalition_dissent -= 4;
    } else if (Q.government_party == "psl") {
        Q.psl_relation += 7;
        Q.psl_coalition_dissent -= 4;
    } else if (Q.government_party == "p2050") {
        Q.p2050_relation += 7;
        Q.p2050_coalition_dissent -= 4;
    } else {
        Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 4;
    }
    Q.razem_dissent += 5;
    Q.progressives_dissent += 3;
    Q.kpo_last_credit_change = -4;
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "The cabinet gains stability; the Left disappears behind " +
        Q.prime_minister + ".";
}
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 1;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.prime_minister + " owns the return to Europe's first rank";
!}

The win is banked centrally and without argument. **[+ prime_minister +]** takes
it to Brussels, takes it to the cameras, and — the part that matters — takes it
into the next coalition negotiation, where a leader who has just closed Article
7 is a leader who is owed something by everyone at the table.

[? if government_party = "lewica": The Chancellery is ours, so the debt is ours to call in. Our negotiators start the December list that afternoon: the care lines first, the housing programme second, and a note beside each one recording what it was traded for.?]
[? if government_party != "lewica": The Chancellery is not ours. We have spent our share of a European achievement buying goodwill for **[+ prime_minister +]**, and in December, when that goodwill is converted into a budget, it will be converted into somebody else's priorities. We knew this when we agreed to it; it was still the cheapest way to keep the cabinet standing.?]

- @kpo_result: Bank the European win

@article7_opposition_truth
title: Welcome the money and list every unresolved domestic institution
subtitle: Applaud the transfer and publish, on the same page, the appointments Article 7 closure did not touch.
view-if: left_in_government = 0 and kpo_article7_reward = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_public_credit += 3;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 2;
Q.pis_relation -= 1;
Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "The government owns the European win; Lewica owns the list of what it did not fix";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 3;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The opposition accepts the European reward without certifying the government's legal record.";
Q.news_headline = "The Left welcomes KPO money and keeps the court ledger open";
!}

We welcome the money and refuse to pretend it certifies anything. Article 7
closed because the political situation changed, not because a Polish court was
put right, and the list of what remains unrepaired goes out on the same page as
the welcome, in the same typeface, at the same hour.

It is a much harder position to hold than either applause or denunciation, and
it is unusable as a slogan. The judges' associations recognise it within a day
and say so. **[+ prime_minister +]** finds an opposition that cannot be accused
of wanting Poland to fail, which is a genuine inconvenience to a government
whose main line about us is precisely that.

- @kpo_result: Welcome it honestly

@article7_pis_conditions
title: Publish every unmet benchmark and the statutes needed to clear it
subtitle: Show the route out of the impasse without pretending Europe has approved it.
view-if: government_party = "pis" and left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 4;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.judicial_repair_mandate += 3;
Q.pis_relation -= 4;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary =
    "Lewica publishes a route out of the impasse without claiming a payment or completed milestone.";
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica lists the conditions still blocking Article 7 and KPO";
!}

We set out exactly what closure would require: the statutes, the appointments
and the disciplinary rules, each with the article number that would have to
change and the length of the amendment that would change it. Most of them are
under a page. It is a route map for a government that has no intention whatever
of walking it.

The point is not to persuade **[+ pis_leader +]**, who is not persuadable on
this and has built four years of politics on not being. The point is that when
the money stays frozen, nobody in Poland will be able to claim honestly that the
conditions were secret, moving, or impossible to meet.

- @kpo_result: Publish the benchmarks

@article7_pis_pressure
title: Make the frozen file a competence case against the PiS cabinet
subtitle: Turn the frozen file into a competence case against PiS, not fictional progress.
view-if: government_party = "pis" and left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.media_capacity += 3;
Q.labor_credibility += 2;
Q.pis_relation -= 6;
Q.ko_relation -= 1;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary =
    "The opposition turns the frozen file into accountability, not fictional European progress.";
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica blames the surviving PiS cabinet for the frozen recovery file";
!}

We stop arguing about sovereignty and start arguing about arithmetic: the
billions not drawn down, the projects that never opened a site office, the
counties that spent two years watching Czech and Slovak neighbours pour
concrete. The file is frozen because ministers in Warsaw chose a fight, and the
bill for it arrives in places that were never asked.

**[+ pis_leader +]** is entirely comfortable defending a constitutional
principle for six hours and visibly uncomfortable defending a road that was
never built. The change of subject is the attack.

Konfederacja notices the opening within a fortnight and starts making the same
argument with the social half removed — the state wasted your money, rather than
the state owes you a bus. That version travels further than ours and costs them
nothing to hold.

- @kpo_result: Make it a competence case


@kpo_budget_gate_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — Ready projects against paper milestones is the right question, the finance minister is a person in the room with a position rather than an abstraction, February's ledger and February's grudge both change the price, and the branches answer honestly: matched money reaching only counties that already had a project office, an unglamorous correction team, and a spreadsheet balanced by moving the problem into next year.
