Q.kpo_grudge_name = String(Q.kpo_grudge_name || "");
Q.kpo_grudge_leader = String(Q.kpo_grudge_leader || "");
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = String(Q.kpo_grudge_reason || "");
// A finance ministry held by a party we took something from is the one place
// in the budget round where February is still being charged for.
Q.kpo_finance_hostile =
    Q.kpo_grudge_active && Q.kpo_grudge_code &&
    String(Q.finance_minister_party || "").trim() ==
        kpoNames24d[Q.kpo_grudge_code]
        ? 1 : 0;
const kpoBudgetReadiness24 =
    Q.kpo_milestones * 2 + Q.kpo_delivery -
    Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - Q.kpo_shortcut_debt * 2;
Q.kpo_review_2024 =
    kpoBudgetReadiness24 >= 15
        ? "Milestones credible"
        : (kpoBudgetReadiness24 >= 4
            ? "Corrective file required"
            : "Next tranche at risk");
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The first full coalition budget must distinguish grants, co-financing and ordinary promises.";
Q.news_headline = "KPO co-financing enters the first full coalition budget";
!}

= December 2024 — Projects must be ready before grants support the budget

Review: **[+ kpo_review_2024 +]**. Tranches released but not yet committed:
**[+ kpo_uncommitted +]**.

The budget round runs for eleven days in a room on Świętokrzyska Street, and it
is not a debate about priorities. It is **[+ finance_minister +]**
([+ finance_minister_party +]) reading each proposed line and asking one
question about it: can this money legally leave the account before August 2026,
and if it cannot, why is it in a budget rather than in a press release.

[? if left_in_government = 1: Twenty months remain. Between the recovery money that has arrived and the projects able to absorb it lies the ordinary state — permits, tenders, an appeal period, a county architect on sick leave — and the budget can either buy its way through that or paper over it for a year.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1 and kpo_ledger_public = 1: February's ledger is on the table, printed, with the late lines highlighted by somebody in the ministry who wanted them highlighted. It is much harder to promise a tranche to a project whose slipped date is already public.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1 and kpo_finance_hostile = 1: The ministry is held by [+ kpo_grudge_name +], and [+ kpo_grudge_leader +] has neither forgotten nor forgiven [+ kpo_grudge_reason +]. Nothing is refused. Everything of ours simply requires one more document than everybody else's.?]
[? if left_in_government = 0: We are not in the room. What we have is the printed budget, the Commission's quarterly absorption figure, and the arithmetic that connects the two — which is more than most of the people voting on it will have read.?]

- @budget_gate_social
- @budget_gate_correction
- @budget_gate_paper
- @budget_gate_opposition

@budget_gate_social
title: Match KPO money with the housing, care and local-service budget
subtitle: [? if kpo_finance_hostile = 1: Spends two released tranches, and every one of them has to be argued past a finance ministry that owes us nothing.?][? if kpo_finance_hostile = 0: Spends two released tranches on the social projects that already have a start date.?]
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: kpo_uncommitted >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Too little unlocked money remains for a matched package.
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_funds_spent += 2;
Q.budget += Q.kpo_finance_hostile ? 1 : 2;
Q.kpo_delivery += Q.kpo_finance_hostile ? 4 : 5;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 4;
Q.government_delivery += 4;
Q.fiscal_stress = Math.max(0, Q.fiscal_stress - 2);
Q.psl_relation += 2;
Q.razem_dissent -= 3;
if (Q.kpo_finance_hostile) {
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 2;
} else {
    Q.kpo_grudge_active = 0;
    Q.kpo_grudge_reason = "";
}
Q.kpo_owner = "lewica";
Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "The matched social lines are Lewica's and carry Lewica's start dates";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 4;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = Q.kpo_finance_hostile ? 4 : 5;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "Ready European projects add real room to the governing budget.";
Q.news_headline = "KPO co-financing protects the coalition's social investment";
!}

Ready European projects go into the domestic budget as matched lines. Housing,
care and local services enter December holding the one thing no other demand in
the room has: a co-financing partner and a date on which work starts.

[? if kpo_finance_hostile = 1: **[+ finance_minister +]** does not refuse. The ministry requests a revised cost annex, then a legal opinion on two of the schemes, then the same legal opinion in a different format, and the package clears on the tenth day with one programme trimmed and everybody's temper gone. February is being invoiced, item by item, and it is being invoiced politely.?]
[? if kpo_finance_hostile = 0: **[+ finance_minister +]** takes them, because refusing free European money in a December budget round is a position no finance minister can hold for eleven days in public. The argument is over in an afternoon.?]

What our own negotiators notice on the way out is which projects were matchable
at all: the ones that were already prepared, in counties that already had
somebody employed to prepare them. Hajnówka is in the package. Two dozen places
poorer than Hajnówka are not, and their reason for not being in it is that
nobody there had the staff to write the application.

- @kpo_result: Match the money

@budget_gate_correction
title: Fund a transparent correction team before promising the tranche
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Nine people, eight weeks, no announcement — and the tranche is not promised to anything until they report.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party lacks the technical and local audit team.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.kpo_milestones += 3;
Q.kpo_delivery += 2;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 3);
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_shortcut_debt - 1);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 1;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 1;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 2;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The correction is not glamorous, but it keeps a weak file financeable.";
Q.news_headline = "The coalition funds a KPO correction before the budget vote";
!}

Nine civil servants and two outside auditors go through the weak annexes before
a złoty of the tranche is promised to anything. They find exactly what such
teams always find: timetables written by optimists, co-financing counted twice
because two ministries each assumed the other had it, and two schemes that
cannot lawfully start until a regulation nobody has drafted is drafted.

The report goes to **[+ finance_minister +]** rather than to the press, which
is the only reason the ministries co-operated with it at all.

Nobody will ever cheer for this and no party conference will ever hear about it.
It is also the difference between a budget resting on money that arrives and a
budget resting on money that a desk officer in Brussels is, at this moment,
preparing to send back with questions.

- @kpo_result: Fund the correction team

@budget_gate_paper
title: Count legal adoption as delivery and protect the ordinary budget
subtitle: [? if kpo_ledger_public = 1: The spreadsheet balances tonight, against dates we published under our own names in February.?][? if kpo_ledger_public = 0: The spreadsheet balances tonight and the implementation risk moves into 2025.?]
