} else {
    Q.kpo_midterm_status = "Payment delayed";
    Q.kpo_funds_status = "Payment delayed; milestones and legality disputed";
    Q.kpo_funds_delayed += 3;
    Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 7;
    Q.fiscal_stress += 3;
    Q.kpo_last_summary = "A delayed payment turns technical debt into a coalition crisis.";
    Q.news_headline = "A KPO payment is delayed as deadlines close in";
}
Q.kpo_uncommitted = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.kpo_funds_available - Q.kpo_funds_spent
);
!}

= October 2025 — The audit after the campaign

Status: **[+ kpo_midterm_status +]**. Uncommitted blocks:
**[+ kpo_uncommitted +]**.

Ten months remain. Not ten months to start things — ten months to finish them,
invoice them and have them certified, which for anything involving concrete
means the decisions that matter are being taken now, in this room, by people who
will not be the ones holding a trowel.

[? if kpo_horeca_seen = 1: The assessors arrive four weeks after the beneficiary map put floating saunas on every front page. Nobody mentions the photographs. Everybody has seen them, and the questions about control systems are noticeably longer than last year's.?]
[? if kpo_horeca_seen = 1: September's answer on the record: **[+ kpo_horeca_line +]**.?]
[? if kpo_horeca_control = 1: That answer built a mechanism rather than a headline, and the mechanism is what the assessors ask to see. It is produced. It works. Four weeks of political misery buy one good afternoon.?]
[? if kpo_horeca_seen = 1 and kpo_horeca_control = 0: What the assessors ask to see is the control system. What exists is a position. The meeting takes an hour longer than scheduled and ends with a request in writing.?]

[? if kpo_midterm_status = "Additional payment cleared": The payment clears. **[+ prime_minister +]** has momentum and a number to say out loud, and neither of those things employs a site inspector in a county that has none.?]
[? if not kpo_midterm_status = "Additional payment cleared": The review turns missed work into fiscal pressure inside a fortnight. **[+ finance_minister +]** wants to know, in writing, which programmes will be cut if the money does not come, and there is no version of that letter that stays confidential.?]

[? if left_in_government = 1 and kpo_grudge_active: **[+ kpo_grudge_leader +]** sits through it saying almost nothing. [+ kpo_grudge_name +] has been waiting since [+ kpo_grudge_reason +] for a meeting where our projects are the ones under review.?]

- @midterm_ready_projects
- @midterm_correction
- @midterm_brand
- @midterm_opposition_support
- @midterm_opposition_audit

