Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "Lewica moved the money and will be named for every project it moved it from";
Q.kpo_grudge_active = 1;
Q.kpo_grudge_code = Q.kpo_partner_code;
Q.kpo_grudge_name = Q.kpo_partner_name;
Q.kpo_grudge_leader = Q.kpo_partner_leader;
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = "the October 2025 reallocation";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 4;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = reallocationEvidenced ? 6 : 5;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "Reallocation trades ministerial ownership for projects that can finish.";
Q.news_headline = "KPO money moves to projects that can still be completed";
!}

Money is taken out of schemes that cannot finish by August and put into
municipal and social projects that can. Every single reallocation has a minister
on the losing end of it, and two of the losing ministers are ours, and one of
those two does not find out until the list is circulated.

[? if kpo_ledger_public = 1: The ledger does the arguing. Each stripped scheme has a published date it has already missed, printed in February over the signature of the ministry that missed it, and there is no version of the objection that does not begin by explaining that date. The meeting takes ninety minutes.?]
[? if kpo_ledger_public = 0: With nothing published, every stripped scheme is a matter of opinion, and the opinion of the ministry losing the money is that its timetable was always achievable. **[+ kpo_partner_leader +]** takes it to the coalition council as a question of trust rather than of dates, which is exactly the argument we cannot win with a spreadsheet.?]

The counties that gain are the ones with a shovel-ready file and a project
officer who answers the telephone in October. The review will record more
completions. Two ministries will record, permanently and to anybody who asks,
that Lewica raided their budgets in order to get them.

- @kpo_result: Move the money

@midterm_correction
title: Sign a coalition correction protocol with measurable deadlines
subtitle: [? if kpo_ledger_public = 1: February's ledger becomes the protocol's schedule; the dates are already public, so only the repairs are new.?][? if kpo_ledger_public = 0: Trade the easy headline for a dated repair plan the coalition has to negotiate from nothing.?]
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
// A coalition that has already published dates is negotiating repairs; one
// that has not spends the same fortnight negotiating what the dates were.
const protocolHasLedger = Q.kpo_ledger_public ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_milestones += protocolHasLedger ? 4 : 3;
Q.kpo_delivery += 3;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - (protocolHasLedger ? 6 : 4)
);
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.kpo_shortcut_debt - (protocolHasLedger ? 3 : 2)
);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 1;
Q.ko_relation += 1;
Q.psl_relation += 1;
Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 2;
Q.kpo_grudge_active = 0;
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = "";
Q.kpo_ledger_public = 1;
Q.kpo_owner = "shared";
Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "A dated coalition protocol binds every partner to a repair, ours included";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 1;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 3;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "A correction protocol steadies the file without producing an instant ribbon-cutting.";
Q.news_headline = "The coalition signs a dated KPO correction protocol";
!}

The coalition signs a repair plan with a date against each item instead of
announcing a rescue. It is deliberately boring — no launch, no backdrop, a
two-page annex — and the dates are deliberately close enough that missing one
will be noticed by somebody outside the building.

[? if kpo_prior_ledger = 1: February's ledger supplies the schedule, so the fortnight is spent arguing about repairs rather than about what was ever promised. **[+ kpo_partner_leader +]** signs on the fourth day; the arithmetic was agreed eighteen months ago and nobody can now claim otherwise.?]
[? if kpo_prior_ledger = 0: Half the fortnight goes on establishing what the original dates even were, because no agreed document has ever said so. Three ministries produce three timetables. The protocol that emerges is real, and it is three weeks late for what it has to do.?]

There is no ribbon to cut this month, and **[+ razem_leader +]** points out that
we have signed away the right to blame anybody else for the next ten months.
That is accurate. What we have in exchange is the first document in the
programme's history against which every partner can be held in public,
ourselves included, before the deadline rather than after it.

- @kpo_result: Sign the protocol

@midterm_brand
title: Centralise the rescue and promise that every project will finish
subtitle: One slogan, one Chancellery, one promise made about projects nobody has re-costed since 2023.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
Q.kpo_delivery += 1;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt += 3;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 2;
Q.public_trust -= 2;
Q.kpo_owner = Q.government_party == "lewica" ? "lewica" : "chancellery";
Q.kpo_owner_label = Q.government_party == "lewica"
    ? "Lewica's Chancellery promised every project would finish"
    : Q.prime_minister + " promised every project would finish";
Q.kpo_grudge_active = 0;
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = "";
if (Q.government_party == "lewica") {
    Q.kpo_public_credit += 2;
    Q.party_unity += 1;
    Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 2;
    Q.psl_coalition_dissent += 1;
    Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 2;
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "Lewica's central control produces a clean slogan and direct ownership of every unfinished project.";
} else {
    Q.kpo_public_credit -= 3;
    if (Q.government_party == "ko") {
        Q.ko_relation += 4;
    } else if (Q.government_party == "psl") {
        Q.psl_relation += 4;
    } else if (Q.government_party == "p2050") {
        Q.p2050_relation += 4;
    }
    Q.razem_dissent += 4;
    Q.kpo_last_credit_change = -3;
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "Central control gives " + Q.prime_minister +
        " a cleaner slogan than implementation record.";
}
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 1;
Q.news_headline = Q.prime_minister + " takes control of the KPO rescue";
!}

One slogan, one Chancellery, one promise: every project in the plan will be
finished. It is a good line, it travels, and a fortnight of coalition
recrimination stops in the afternoon it is delivered. Those are not small
things, and they are the strongest argument anybody makes for it.

It is also a promise about projects nobody has re-costed since 2023. The
department knows how many are behind. Nobody in the room asks for the figure,
because the promise has already been drafted and a figure would make it
undeliverable.

**[+ prime_minister +]** now owns each of those projects individually, by name,
and so does every party that stood behind the podium while the sentence was
said. In July there will be a list of the ones that did not finish, and this is
the week that decides whose list it is.

- @kpo_result: Centralise the rescue

@midterm_opposition_support
title: Support a narrow corrective act for labour and local projects
subtitle: Supply votes for a narrow repair while leaving implementation with the cabinet.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 2;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 2;
Q.ko_relation += 3;
Q.psl_relation += 2;
Q.labor_credibility += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 2;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "A conditional passage vote wins practical credit; it does not implement the correction for the cabinet.";
Q.news_headline = "The Left supplies votes for a narrow KPO correction";
!}

We vote for the narrow corrective act because the labour projects and the
municipal works are inside it, and we say from the rostrum, before the vote and
not after, that we are voting for those and not for **[+ prime_minister +]**'s
stewardship of anything.

The act passes with our thirty-odd votes inside it. **[+ kpo_partner_leader +]**
thanks the chamber in general terms, and not one report the following morning
records where the majority actually came from.

Implementation stays entirely with a cabinet we do not sit in. We have taken
responsibility for the vote and none whatever for the result — which is honest,
which is useful to about four hundred thousand people, and which cannot be put
on a poster in any language.

- @kpo_result: Supply the votes

@midterm_opposition_audit
title: Refuse a rescue until contracts and missed milestones are published
subtitle: A clean demand, made at the point in the calendar where refusing costs somebody else a building.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_public_credit += Q.kpo_opposition_file ? 5 : 4;
Q.media_capacity += 3;
Q.ko_relation -= 5;
Q.psl_relation -= 2;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 2;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = Q.kpo_opposition_file ? 5 : 4;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The audit line is politically clear and leaves the payment clock running.";
Q.news_headline = "The Left demands the missing KPO contracts before a rescue vote";
!}

No rescue votes until the contracts and the missed milestones are published in
full. The demand is clean, entirely defensible, and explicable at any doorstep
in the country in one sentence — which is more than can be said for anything
else in this programme.

[? if kpo_opposition_file = 1: It is also credible, because our own monitoring team has been publishing a version of that list since 2024 and the government's silence is measurable against it.?]
[? if kpo_opposition_file = 0: The weakness is that we are demanding a document we have never attempted to assemble ourselves, and **[+ prime_minister +]**'s press office says so within the hour.?]

The payment clock does not pause while we hold the line. Mayors with half-built
projects understand the principle perfectly, agree with it, and would still
rather have the money, and two of them say exactly that on regional television
with a foundation slab behind them.

- @kpo_result: Demand the contracts


@kpo_budget_gate_2025
# prose-audit: Grade A — The binding constraint is now a person: the county with an approved project, no building inspector and eight months left. All four routes are written through to their cost, and the premise stands somebody on the bridge instead of describing it.
title: The recovery-fund budget bridge
subtitle: Eight months left, and the constraint is not money — it is the people who sign things.
face-image: img/poland/events/kpo.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 12
order: 80
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month = 12
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_funds_available =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_available))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_funds_available)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_funds_spent =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_spent))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_funds_spent)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_delivery =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_delivery))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_delivery)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_public_credit =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_public_credit))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_public_credit)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_deadline_pressure))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_deadline_pressure) + 3
        : 11;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_shortcut_debt))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_shortcut_debt)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_funds_delayed =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_delayed))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_funds_delayed)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_uncommitted = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.kpo_funds_available - Q.kpo_funds_spent
);
const kpoNames25b = {
    ko: "KO",
    p2050: "Poland 2050",
    psl: "PSL",
    pis: "PiS",
    konf: "Konfederacja"
};
const kpoSeats25b = function(code) {
    return Q["ministry_" + code + "_in_cabinet"]
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q[code + "_seats"]) || 0)
        : 0;
};
Q.kpo_partner_code = Object.keys(kpoNames25b)
    .filter(function(code) { return kpoSeats25b(code) > 0; })
    .sort(function(first, second) {
        return (second == Q.government_party ? 1e6 : kpoSeats25b(second)) -
            (first == Q.government_party ? 1e6 : kpoSeats25b(first));
    })[0] || "";
Q.kpo_partner_name =
    kpoNames25b[Q.kpo_partner_code] || "the coalition's other parties";
Q.kpo_partner_leader =
    String(Q[Q.kpo_partner_code + "_leader"] || "").trim() ||
    String(Q.prime_minister || "the senior partner");
Q.kpo_ledger_public = Q.kpo_ledger_public ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_prior_ledger = Q.kpo_ledger_public;
Q.kpo_opposition_file = Q.kpo_opposition_file ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_owner = String(Q.kpo_owner || "none");
Q.kpo_prior_owner = Q.kpo_owner;
Q.kpo_grudge_active = Q.kpo_grudge_active ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_grudge_name = String(Q.kpo_grudge_name || "");
Q.kpo_grudge_leader = String(Q.kpo_grudge_leader || "");
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = String(Q.kpo_grudge_reason || "");
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The budget must fund the institutions that turn milestones into completed work.";
Q.news_headline = "KPO completion becomes a line in the 2026 budget";
!}

= December 2025 — Fund completion or hide the delay

Available but uncommitted: **[+ kpo_uncommitted +]** blocks. Deadline pressure:
**[+ kpo_deadline_pressure +]**.

The 2026 budget is drafted against a wall. Eight months from now the programme
stops, and anything not finished, invoiced and certified by then is money
returned to Brussels with a covering letter.

The constraint at this point is not the money and everybody in the room knows
it. There are counties holding an approved grant, a signed contract and a
building site that cannot proceed because the one person entitled to sign the
next document works three days a week and is currently signing something else.
That is what stands between a grant and a clinic in December 2025: a post, a
salary, a person.

[? if left_in_government = 1: **[+ finance_minister +]** would rather spend the same money on the deficit line, and the argument for that is not stupid — a reserve is certain, and an inspector hired in January is a bet that the thing being inspected gets built by August.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1 and kpo_grudge_active: [+ kpo_grudge_name +] arrives at the table still holding [+ kpo_grudge_reason +], and prices it into every request we make this month.?]
[? if left_in_government = 0: From outside the cabinet none of this is ours to fund. What we can do is decide what our cooperation on the budget costs, and absorption is the one number the government cannot argue with, because the Commission publishes it quarterly.?]

- @bridge_enforcement
- @bridge_reserve
- @bridge_defer
- @bridge_opposition

@bridge_enforcement
title: Fund inspectors, permitting teams and local co-financing
subtitle: Spends two released tranches on salaries. Nothing opens, nothing is announced, and the sites move.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: kpo_uncommitted >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The unlocked reserve is already committed.
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_funds_spent += 2;
Q.budget += 2;
Q.kpo_delivery += 5;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 3);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 3;
Q.public_sector_support += 3;
Q.local_network += 2;
Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "Lewica bought eight months of administrative capacity and no photographs";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 3;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 5;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "Administrative capacity turns European money into usable budget room.";
Q.news_headline = "The budget funds the people required to finish KPO projects";
!}

The money goes on building inspectors, permitting officers and the local
co-financing desks that turn an approved project into a signed contract with a
contractor standing next to it. It is the least photogenic use of a European
recovery fund that anybody in this coalition has yet proposed.

It is also the binding constraint, and it is a solvable one. A large part of the
delay in this programme has been municipalities with a grant and no employee
qualified to complete the next form — which is, unusually for this file, a
problem that money genuinely fixes.

**[+ finance_minister +]** signs it off on the understanding that these are
temporary posts. They will not be temporary. The counties that get a permitting
officer in January will fight to keep one in 2027, and they will be right to,
and the bill for that will land on somebody who is not in this room tonight.

- @kpo_result: Fund the staff

@bridge_reserve
title: Keep a smaller corrective reserve behind the budget
subtitle: The safe option. It insures the budget against the failure instead of preventing it.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.budget += 1;
Q.kpo_delivery += 1;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 1;
Q.fiscal_stress = Math.max(0, Q.fiscal_stress - 1);
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.psl_relation += 1;
Q.kpo_grudge_active = 0;
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = "";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 1;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 1;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The reserve protects fiscal room, but cannot finish many projects by itself.";
Q.news_headline = "The coalition keeps a KPO correction reserve";
!}

A smaller reserve is held back to protect the budget, and it will protect the
budget. **[+ finance_minister +]** is satisfied and stops asking for the letter
about which programmes would be cut. The completion risk the reserve does not
cover is left exactly where it was found.

We have chosen fiscal safety over finishing the work, knowingly, with the
figures in front of us. Nobody in the room pretends otherwise, which is at least
an improvement on last year.

When projects fail to complete next summer — and some will — this reserve will
be the reason that failure does not also become a budget crisis. It will not
have prevented a single one of the failures. It was never going to. It was
chosen because it is certain and the alternative was a bet.

- @kpo_result: Keep the reserve

@bridge_defer
title: Protect the headline budget and push implementation into 2026
subtitle: The last year available. Whatever moves into it cannot be moved again.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 6;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt += 2;
Q.kpo_delivery -= 2;
Q.kpo_public_credit -= 3;
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.razem_dissent += 5;
Q.labor_credibility -= 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = -3;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = -2;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The ordinary budget looks safer and the recovery deadline becomes harsher.";
Q.news_headline = "The coalition defers KPO implementation into its final year";
!}

The ordinary budget comes through December looking sound, which was the
objective and which is worth something in a year with an election in it. The
unfinished work goes into 2026 — the last year available, and therefore the
year in which nothing can be deferred a second time.

**[+ kpo_partner_leader +]** is relieved and says so privately.
**[+ razem_leader +]** is not and says so on the record, at length, using the
word that the whole coalition has spent two years avoiding, which is *returned*.

Everyone at the table understands the trade precisely. The people who will
actually have to administer it — a county architect in Podlaskie, a
project officer on a nine-month contract — are not at the table and will read
about it in January.

- @kpo_result: Protect the headline

@bridge_opposition
title: Make KPO absorption a condition for any budget favour
subtitle: One number, published quarterly by the Commission, that the government cannot dispute or delay.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_public_credit += 3;
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 2;
Q.psl_relation += 1;
Q.labor_credibility += 2;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 3;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The opposition converts a technical deadline into a visible condition for cooperation.";
Q.news_headline = "The Left ties every budget favour to KPO absorption";
!}

We name the price and it is a number: no cooperation on any part of this budget
until the government states what proportion of the fund has actually been drawn
down and spent. Not committed. Not allocated. Spent.

The choice of measure is the whole tactic. **[+ finance_minister +]** can refuse
us, and the refusal cannot be made quietly, because the absorption figure is
published quarterly by the Commission in a table anybody with an internet
connection can open — including every mayor whose project is in it.

What we have not done is say what we would do with the money instead, and by
February somebody will ask.

- @kpo_result: Set the condition


@kpo_pip_milestone_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — Vote, signature and enforcement stay distinct, the division list carries two years of coalition credit fights into the count, and the aftermaths follow the distinction into labour courts taking the load, a specialist team with an expiry date, and a milestone legible in Brussels and hollow at the workplace.
title: The PIP milestone reaches its legal test
subtitle: A bill about junk contracts, decided by a majority we spent two years spending.
face-image: img/poland/events/kpo.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 26
order: 20
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 4 and labor_reform_settled = 0
call: poland_senate.refresh
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones = Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_milestones))
    ? Number(Q.kpo_milestones) : 0;
Q.kpo_delivery =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_delivery)) ? Number(Q.kpo_delivery) : 0;
Q.kpo_funds_available =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_available))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_funds_available)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_funds_spent =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_spent))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_funds_spent)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_deadline_pressure))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_deadline_pressure)
        : 10;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_shortcut_debt))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_shortcut_debt)
        : 0;
const kpoNames26 = {
    ko: "KO",
    p2050: "Poland 2050",
    psl: "PSL",
    pis: "PiS",
    konf: "Konfederacja"
};
const kpoSeats26 = function(code) {
    return Q["ministry_" + code + "_in_cabinet"]
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q[code + "_seats"]) || 0)
        : 0;
};
Q.kpo_partner_code = Object.keys(kpoNames26)
    .filter(function(code) { return kpoSeats26(code) > 0; })
    .sort(function(first, second) {
        return (second == Q.government_party ? 1e6 : kpoSeats26(second)) -
            (first == Q.government_party ? 1e6 : kpoSeats26(first));
    })[0] || "";
Q.kpo_partner_name =
    kpoNames26[Q.kpo_partner_code] || "the coalition's other parties";
Q.kpo_partner_leader =
    String(Q[Q.kpo_partner_code + "_leader"] || "").trim() ||
    String(Q.prime_minister || "the senior partner");
Q.kpo_ledger_public = Q.kpo_ledger_public ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_prior_ledger = Q.kpo_ledger_public;
Q.kpo_opposition_file = Q.kpo_opposition_file ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_owner = String(Q.kpo_owner || "none");
Q.kpo_prior_owner = Q.kpo_owner;
Q.kpo_grudge_active = Q.kpo_grudge_active ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_grudge_name = String(Q.kpo_grudge_name || "");
Q.kpo_grudge_leader = String(Q.kpo_grudge_leader || "");
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = String(Q.kpo_grudge_reason || "");
const pipSejmTotal = Number(Q.sejm_total) || 460;
const pipRecordedGovernmentSupport = Number(Q.government_support_seats);
const pipCoalitionWithoutLeft = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.coalition_seats) || 0) -
        (Q.left_in_government
            ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.ministry_left_cabinet_seats) || 0)
            : 0)
);
const pipGovernmentBaseVotes =
    Q.government_has_confidence && !Q.caretaker_government
        ? (
            Number.isFinite(pipRecordedGovernmentSupport)
                ? Math.max(0, pipRecordedGovernmentSupport)
                : pipCoalitionWithoutLeft
        )
        : 0;
// An unsettled KPO credit fight is paid for here. A partner whose ministries we
// raided and never compensated does not vote the bill down; it simply declines
// to whip, and four of its deputies find somewhere else to be.
Q.pip_grudge_defections = Q.kpo_grudge_active && Q.left_in_government ? 4 : 0;
Q.pip_coalition_defections = Math.min(
    pipGovernmentBaseVotes,
    Math.max(
        0,
        Math.round(
            ((Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 30) / 7
        ) + Q.pip_grudge_defections
    )
);
const pipGovernmentVotes = Math.max(
    0,
    pipGovernmentBaseVotes - Q.pip_coalition_defections
);
const pipLeftVotes = Math.max(
    0,
    Number(Q.left_committed_seats) || Number(Q.left_seats) || 0
);
Q.pip_sejm_yes = Math.min(
    pipSejmTotal,
    Math.round(pipGovernmentVotes + pipLeftVotes)
);
const pipOppositionPool = Math.max(0, pipSejmTotal - Q.pip_sejm_yes);
Q.pip_sejm_absent = Math.min(
    pipOppositionPool,
    Math.max(8, Math.round(pipSejmTotal * 0.02))
);
Q.pip_sejm_abstain = Math.min(
    Math.max(0, pipOppositionPool - Q.pip_sejm_absent),
    Math.round(pipOppositionPool * 0.06)
);
Q.pip_sejm_no = Math.max(
    0,
    pipSejmTotal - Q.pip_sejm_yes -
        Q.pip_sejm_absent - Q.pip_sejm_abstain
);
Q.pip_sejm_present =
    Q.pip_sejm_yes + Q.pip_sejm_no + Q.pip_sejm_abstain;
Q.pip_sejm_quorum = Math.ceil(pipSejmTotal / 2);
Q.pip_sejm_threshold = Q.pip_sejm_no + 1;
Q.pip_sejm_passed =
    Q.pip_sejm_present >= Q.pip_sejm_quorum &&
    Q.pip_sejm_yes > Q.pip_sejm_no ? 1 : 0;
const pipSenateTotal = Math.max(
    1,
    Math.round(Number(Q.senate_total) || 100)
);
const pipSenateThreshold = Math.floor(pipSenateTotal / 2) + 1;
// The scene's `call:` refresh completes after this arrival block, so calculate
// cabinet membership from live party/portfolio state rather than stale cache.
const pipCabinetSenators = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(
        pipSenateTotal,
        (Q.government_party == "pis"
            ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_pis_seats) || 0) : 0) +
        (
            Q.government_party == "ko" || Q.ministry_ko_in_cabinet
                ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_ko_seats) || 0) : 0
        ) +
        (
            Q.government_party == "p2050" || Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet
                ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_p2050_seats) || 0) : 0
        ) +
        (
            Q.government_party == "psl" || Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet
                ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_psl_seats) || 0) : 0
        ) +
        (
            Q.government_party == "lewica" || Q.left_in_government
                ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_left_seats) || 0) : 0
        )
    )
);
const pipLeftSenators = Q.left_in_government
    ? 0
    : Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.senate_left_seats) || 0));
const pipIndependentSenators = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.round(Number(Q.senate_independent_seats) || 0)
);
const pipIndependentSupport = Math.round(
    pipIndependentSenators *
        Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Number(Q.public_trust) || 0)) / 100
);
Q.pip_senate_yes = Q.pip_sejm_passed
    ? Math.min(
        pipSenateTotal,
        pipCabinetSenators + pipLeftSenators + pipIndependentSupport
    )
    : 0;
Q.pip_senate_no = Q.pip_sejm_passed
    ? Math.max(0, pipSenateTotal - Q.pip_senate_yes)
    : 0;
Q.pip_senate_threshold = pipSenateThreshold;
Q.pip_senate_action = !Q.pip_sejm_passed
    ? "No Senate review"
    : (
        Q.pip_senate_yes < pipSenateThreshold
            ? "Senate rejected the bill"
            : (
                pipCabinetSenators >= pipSenateThreshold
                    ? "Senate accepted the bill without amendment"
                    : "Senate adopted a worker-appeals amendment"
            )
    );
Q.pip_senate_return_yes = 0;
Q.pip_senate_return_threshold = 0;
Q.pip_senate_return_passed = 0;
let pipParliamentPassed = Boolean(Q.pip_sejm_passed);
if (
    Q.pip_senate_action == "Senate rejected the bill" ||
    Q.pip_senate_action == "Senate adopted a worker-appeals amendment"
) {
    Q.pip_senate_return_yes = Q.pip_sejm_yes;
    Q.pip_senate_return_threshold =
        Math.floor(Q.pip_sejm_present / 2) + 1;
    Q.pip_senate_return_passed =
        Q.pip_senate_return_yes >= Q.pip_senate_return_threshold ? 1 : 0;
    if (Q.pip_senate_action == "Senate rejected the bill") {
        pipParliamentPassed = Boolean(Q.pip_senate_return_passed);
    }
}
Q.pip_parliament_passed = pipParliamentPassed ? 1 : 0;
const pipRightWingPresident = [
    "Andrzej Duda",
    String(Q.pres_2025_right_candidate || ""),
    "Sławomir Mentzen",
    "Grzegorz Braun"
].includes(Q.president_name);
const pipHostilePresident =
    (
        pipRightWingPresident ||
        (
            Q.pres_2025_hostile_president &&
            Q.president_name == Q.pres_2025_winner
        )
    ) &&
    Q.government_party != "pis";
const pipVeto =
    Q.pip_parliament_passed &&
    pipHostilePresident &&
    (Number(Q.president_relation) || 0) < 45;
Q.pip_law_enacted = Q.pip_parliament_passed && !pipVeto ? 1 : 0;
Q.pip_presidential_action = !Q.pip_parliament_passed
    ? "No bill reached the President"
    : (pipVeto ? "Presidential veto" : "Signed into law");
if (Q.pip_law_enacted) {
    Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "The enacted inspection reform records a legal milestone; enforcement remains open.";
    Q.news_headline =
        "The PIP reform passes, is signed and moves to enforcement";
} else if (pipVeto) {
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        "A presidential veto blocks the legal milestone before implementation.";
    Q.news_headline = "The President vetoes the PIP milestone bill";
} else {
    Q.kpo_last_summary =
        Q.pip_sejm_passed
            ? "The Senate procedure stops the PIP bill before presidential action."
            : "The PIP bill lacks a Sejm majority and records no milestone.";
    Q.news_headline = Q.pip_sejm_passed
        ? "The PIP milestone bill fails during Senate review"
        : "The PIP milestone bill fails in the Sejm";
}
Q.kpo_uncommitted = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.kpo_funds_available - Q.kpo_funds_spent
);
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 0;
!}

= April 2026 — A milestone at the workplace

The bill is about a document. Somewhere between one and two million people in
Poland work under a civil-law contract that describes them as an independent
contractor and a labour inspector would describe as an employee: fixed hours, a
supervisor, a uniform, no sick pay. The milestone requires the State Labour
Inspection to be able to reclassify those contracts without first going to
court, and **[+ labor_minister +]** has been carrying the text since January.

Four months remain before the programme closes. This is the last legislative
milestone in the plan that has an identifiable Polish workplace behind it, and
it has to clear three separate hurdles that the public will hear about as one
event: a Sejm majority, the Senate, and a signature.

[? if pip_law_enacted: It clears all three. The Inspection acquires, on paper, a power it has wanted since the 1990s. Recording that as a European milestone takes one afternoon; producing the thousands of inspections, appeals and converted contracts it is supposed to describe takes people who have not been hired.?]
[? if not pip_law_enacted: The proposal receives **[+ pip_sejm_yes +] yes** against **[+ pip_sejm_no +] no**, with **[+ pip_sejm_abstain +] abstentions** and **[+ pip_sejm_absent +] absent**. It needed **[+ pip_sejm_threshold +] yes** among the votes cast and a quorum of **[+ pip_sejm_quorum +]**.?]

Senate: **[+ pip_senate_action +]** (**[+ pip_senate_yes +]–[+
pip_senate_no +]**). [? if pip_senate_return_threshold > 0: The Sejm return vote records **[+ pip_senate_return_yes +] yes** against an absolute-majority threshold of **[+ pip_senate_return_threshold +]**.?] Presidential result:
**[+ pip_presidential_action +]**, from **[+ president_name +]**. No milestone
and no inspector's power exists until every stage of that sentence is complete.

[? if pip_coalition_defections > 0: **[+ pip_coalition_defections +] expected government votes** are missing from the count. They are not recorded as opposition; they are coalition deputies who found something else to do on a Thursday afternoon, and every one of them was whipped by somebody who chose not to whip hard.?]
[? if pip_grudge_defections > 0: Four of them belong to [+ kpo_grudge_name +]. **[+ kpo_grudge_leader +]** has never been paid for [+ kpo_grudge_reason +], has waited a long time for a vote where it would matter, and did not have to say a word to anybody to collect.?]

- @pip_full_enforcement
- @pip_kpo_team
- @pip_paper
- @pip_opposition
- @pip_revise_bill
- @pip_opposition_campaign

@pip_full_enforcement
title: Fund inspectors, appeal capacity and worker legal aid
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget capacity.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and pip_law_enacted = 1
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The government budget has no room for recurring enforcement.
on-arrival: {!
Q.budget -= 1;
Q.kpo_delivery += 6;
Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 4);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 5;
Q.labor_credibility += 6;
Q.public_sector_support += 3;
Q.court_backlog += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 5;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 6;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The milestone becomes workplace power, with a manageable new burden on courts.";
Q.news_headline = "Inspectors receive the staff to enforce the KPO labour reform";
!}

Inspectors, appeal capacity and legal aid for workers are funded in one
decision, because an inspectorate without an appeals route produces findings
rather than outcomes, and a worker without a lawyer produces neither.
**[+ labor_minister +]** signs the recruitment schedule the same week.

Employers who have been reclassifying staff for a decade begin receiving visits
in the second month. Most of them are not villains and several are genuinely
astonished; the practice is so normal in three sectors that nobody involved had
thought of it as a decision.

The labour courts take the load, and they were slow before this. They will be
slower. The difference is what is now moving through them: cases that, until
April, would never have been brought by anybody at all.

- @kpo_result: Fund the inspectorate

@pip_kpo_team
title: Use the remaining KPO block for a specialist enforcement team
subtitle: Spends one released tranche on early enforcement before national capacity exists.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and pip_law_enacted = 1
choose-if: kpo_uncommitted >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No unlocked recovery block remains.
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_funds_spent += 1;
Q.kpo_delivery += 4;
Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 3);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 3;
Q.labor_credibility += 4;
Q.court_backlog += 1;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 3;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 4;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "A specialist team produces credible early enforcement without full national capacity.";
Q.news_headline = "KPO technical money launches the PIP enforcement team";
!}

A specialist unit is stood up on the last of the European money: forty people,
paid properly, pointed at the three sectors where reclassification is most
systematic rather than at the whole economy. It will produce real cases, with
names and employers attached, inside six months.

It is not a national capability and nobody in the room should be allowed to
call it one in public. It covers a fraction of the workplaces the law now
touches, chosen deliberately for visibility.

The European money ends in August. This team ends with it unless the 2027
domestic budget adopts the payroll — which is next year's argument, and the
strongest card in it will be forty inspectors with a caseload, which is why the
unit was designed to have one.

- @kpo_result: Build the team

@pip_paper
title: Issue guidance, record the milestone and postpone staffing
subtitle: Give Brussels a legible milestone and workers an inspectorate without staff.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and pip_law_enacted = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones += 4;
Q.kpo_delivery -= 3;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt += 5;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 2;
Q.kpo_public_credit -= 4;
Q.labor_credibility -= 6;
Q.razem_dissent += 8;
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = -4;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = -3;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The milestone is legible in Brussels and hollow at the workplace.";
Q.news_headline = "The PIP milestone passes without an enforcement budget";
!}

The guidance is issued, the milestone is recorded, Brussels is satisfied and
the file closes. Legally, the State Labour Inspection now holds a power it did
not hold last month, and the wording of that power is genuinely good — our
lawyers drafted it.

Practically, the Inspection has the same number of inspectors it had last month
and the same backlog it had last year. **[+ razem_leader +]** reads the
recruitment annex out loud at the party council, because there isn't one.

The workers this milestone was written for will discover, individually and over
about two years, that the protection exists and that nobody has been employed to
give it to them. Some of them will conclude that the law is a lie. They will be
describing this decision accurately.

- @kpo_result: Record the milestone

@pip_opposition
title: Audit converted contracts, appeals and inspector vacancies
subtitle: Count protected workers and vacancies; the cabinet still has to hire the inspectors.
view-if: left_in_government = 0 and pip_law_enacted = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_public_credit += 4;
Q.labor_credibility += 5;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 3;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 4;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The audit makes implementation, not signature, the measure of the milestone.";
Q.news_headline = "The Left counts workers protected by the PIP reform";
!}

We count the three things the government would much rather report in aggregate:
contracts actually converted, appeals actually heard, inspector posts actually
filled. Each is a number. Each is obtainable. None of them is in the ministry's
own press release, which reports the law.

Signature is not implementation, and from this month the distance between them
is a published figure with a date on it.

**[+ labor_minister +]** retains every power needed to close that gap and will
be asked about it monthly. What the audit removes is the option of calling the
milestone complete while the vacancies stand — and the vacancies are the only
part of this that a worker in a warehouse can feel.

- @kpo_result: Publish the audit

@pip_revise_bill
title: Negotiate a narrower bill and return it to Parliament
subtitle: Narrow the bill and return to Parliament without claiming a milestone.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and pip_law_enacted = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.pip_reform_pending = 1;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 2);
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 3;
Q.president_relation += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary =
    "A narrower PIP bill remains pending; no legal milestone is claimed.";
Q.news_headline =
    "The cabinet reopens the PIP bill instead of claiming a fictional milestone";
!}

The bill goes back to committee stripped of the clauses that lost it the vote:
the presumption of employment goes, the penalty schedule is halved, and what
survives is an inspection power with a court stage in front of it. It is
genuinely weaker. It is also genuinely passable, and we say both of those things
out loud rather than presenting the retreat as a refinement.

No milestone can be claimed for a bill that has not passed, and none is claimed.
**[+ labor_minister +]** takes the narrowed text to the union side personally,
which is the correct way to do it and does not make the meeting shorter.

They accept, because the alternative on the table is nothing and August is four
months away. They also write down who asked them to accept it, and that note
will be produced at a congress within the year.

- @kpo_result: Return the narrower bill

@pip_opposition_campaign
title: Publish the failed roll call and organise for a new bill
subtitle: Keep the failed bill alive through workers and the recorded roll call.
view-if: left_in_government = 0 and pip_law_enacted = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.pip_reform_pending = 1;
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 3;
Q.labor_credibility += 3;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary =
    "Opposition pressure keeps the bill alive without pretending it passed.";
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left publishes the failed PIP vote and organises a new bill";
!}

Every name and every vote goes out, matched to the constituency and then to the
warehouses, kitchens and care homes inside it where the contract in question is
standard. The bill is dead. The division list is not, and unlike the bill it
cannot be amended.

Organisers get something specific to hold: not a programme, a name and a
Thursday. Several deputies who assumed the vote would disappear into the
parliamentary record discover instead that it has acquired a local address, a
leaflet and a shift pattern.

**[+ prime_minister +]**'s office complains that this is not how a
recovery-fund milestone is supposed to be discussed. That is true. There was no
milestone.

- @kpo_result: Publish the roll call


@kpo_final_window_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — A genuine trilemma at the deadline — finish what can finish, claim less and have it verified, or certify everything and hand the problem to auditors — with two and a half years of ownership fights arriving at the same table, and each branch stating plainly whose problem it becomes afterwards.
title: The last KPO summer
subtitle: 31 August. Whatever is not certified by then is not late — it is returned.
face-image: img/poland/events/kpo.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 24
order: 30
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 7
call: poland_senate.refresh
on-arrival: {!
const kpoFinalNum = function(value, fallback) {
    return Number.isFinite(Number(value)) ? Number(value) : fallback;
};
Q.kpo_delivery = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_delivery, 0);
Q.kpo_milestones = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_milestones, 0);
Q.kpo_funds_available = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_funds_available, 0);
Q.kpo_funds_spent = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_funds_spent, 0);
Q.kpo_public_credit = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_public_credit, 0);
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_deadline_pressure, 10) + 4;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_shortcut_debt, 0);
Q.kpo_funds_delayed = kpoFinalNum(Q.kpo_funds_delayed, 0);
Q.pip_final_retry_resolved = 0;
Q.pip_final_retry_status = "No PIP revision was pending";
if (Q.pip_reform_pending) {
    Q.pip_final_retry_resolved = 1;
    if (Q.left_in_government) {
        const pipRetryTotal = Number(Q.sejm_total) || 460;
        const pipRetryNoBefore = Number(Q.pip_sejm_no) || 0;
        const pipRetryShift = Math.min(8, pipRetryNoBefore);
        const pipRetryYes = Math.min(
            pipRetryTotal,
            (Number(Q.pip_sejm_yes) || 0) + pipRetryShift
        );
        const pipRetryNo = Math.max(
            0,
            pipRetryNoBefore - pipRetryShift
        );
        const pipRetryPresent =
            pipRetryYes + pipRetryNo + (Number(Q.pip_sejm_abstain) || 0);
        const pipRetryRightPresident = [
            "Andrzej Duda",
            String(Q.pres_2025_right_candidate || ""),
            "Sławomir Mentzen",
            "Grzegorz Braun"
        ].includes(Q.president_name);
        const pipRetryHostile =
            (
                pipRetryRightPresident ||
                (
                    Q.pres_2025_hostile_president &&
                    Q.president_name == Q.pres_2025_winner
                )
            ) &&
            Q.government_party != "pis" &&
            (Number(Q.president_relation) || 0) < 45;
        const pipRetryPassed =
            pipRetryPresent >= Math.ceil(pipRetryTotal / 2) &&
            pipRetryYes > pipRetryNo;
        Q.pip_sejm_yes = pipRetryYes;
        Q.pip_sejm_no = pipRetryNo;
        Q.pip_sejm_present = pipRetryPresent;
        Q.pip_sejm_quorum = Math.ceil(pipRetryTotal / 2);
        Q.pip_sejm_threshold = pipRetryNo + 1;
        Q.pip_sejm_passed = pipRetryPassed ? 1 : 0;
        const retrySenateTotal = Math.max(
            1,
            Math.round(Number(Q.senate_total) || 100)
        );
        const retrySenateThreshold =
            Math.floor(retrySenateTotal / 2) + 1;
        const retryCabinetSenators = Math.max(
            0,
            Math.min(
                retrySenateTotal,
                (Q.government_party == "pis"
                    ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_pis_seats) || 0) : 0) +
                (
                    Q.government_party == "ko" ||
                    Q.ministry_ko_in_cabinet
                        ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_ko_seats) || 0) : 0
                ) +
                (
                    Q.government_party == "p2050" ||
                    Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet
                        ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_p2050_seats) || 0) : 0
                ) +
                (
                    Q.government_party == "psl" ||
                    Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet
                        ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_psl_seats) || 0) : 0
                ) +
                (
                    Q.government_party == "lewica" || Q.left_in_government
                        ? Math.round(Number(Q.senate_left_seats) || 0) : 0
                )
            )
        );
        const retryLeftSenators = Q.left_in_government
            ? 0
            : Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.senate_left_seats) || 0));
        const retryIndependentSupport = Math.round(
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.senate_independent_seats) || 0) *
                Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Number(Q.public_trust) || 0)) /
                100
        );
        Q.pip_senate_yes = pipRetryPassed
            ? Math.min(
                retrySenateTotal,
                retryCabinetSenators + retryLeftSenators +
                    retryIndependentSupport
            )
            : 0;
        Q.pip_senate_no = pipRetryPassed
            ? Math.max(0, retrySenateTotal - Q.pip_senate_yes)
            : 0;
        Q.pip_senate_threshold = retrySenateThreshold;
        Q.pip_senate_action = !pipRetryPassed
            ? "No Senate review"
            : (
                Q.pip_senate_yes < retrySenateThreshold
                    ? "Senate rejected the narrow revision"
                    : (
                        retryCabinetSenators >= retrySenateThreshold
                            ? "Senate accepted the narrow revision"
                            : "Senate amended the narrow revision"
                    )
            );
        Q.pip_senate_return_yes = 0;
        Q.pip_senate_return_threshold = 0;
        Q.pip_senate_return_passed = 0;
        let pipRetryParliamentPassed = Boolean(pipRetryPassed);
        if (
            Q.pip_senate_action == "Senate rejected the narrow revision" ||
            Q.pip_senate_action == "Senate amended the narrow revision"
        ) {
            Q.pip_senate_return_yes = pipRetryYes;
            Q.pip_senate_return_threshold =
                Math.floor(pipRetryPresent / 2) + 1;
            Q.pip_senate_return_passed =
                pipRetryYes >= Q.pip_senate_return_threshold ? 1 : 0;
            if (
                Q.pip_senate_action ==
                    "Senate rejected the narrow revision"
            ) {
                pipRetryParliamentPassed =
                    Boolean(Q.pip_senate_return_passed);
            }
        }
        Q.pip_parliament_passed = pipRetryParliamentPassed ? 1 : 0;
        if (pipRetryParliamentPassed && !pipRetryHostile) {
            Q.pip_law_enacted = 1;
            Q.pip_presidential_action = "Narrow revision signed into law";
            Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
            Q.kpo_delivery += 1;
            Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(
                0,
                Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 2
            );
            Q.pip_final_retry_status =
                "The narrower PIP revision passed and was signed before the final review";
        } else if (pipRetryParliamentPassed) {
            Q.pip_presidential_action = "Narrow revision vetoed";
            Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 3;
            Q.pip_final_retry_status =
                "The narrower PIP revision passed the Sejm but met another presidential veto";
        } else {
            Q.pip_presidential_action = pipRetryPassed
                ? "Narrow revision stopped in Senate procedure"
                : "Narrow revision failed in the Sejm";
            Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 3;
            Q.pip_final_retry_status = pipRetryPassed
                ? "The narrower PIP revision passed the Sejm but did not complete Senate procedure"
                : "The narrower PIP revision returned to the Sejm and failed";
        }
    } else {
        Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 2;
        Q.pip_final_retry_status =
            "The opposition PIP bill received no government time before the KPO deadline";
    }
    Q.pip_reform_pending = 0;
}
const kpoFinalRestraint =
    kpoFinalNum(Q.government_procedural_restraint, 45);
const kpoFinalDualism = kpoFinalNum(Q.legal_dualism, 50);
const kpoFinalScore =
    Q.kpo_milestones * 2 + Q.kpo_delivery * 3 +
    Q.kpo_funds_spent * 2 + kpoFinalRestraint * 0.1 -
    Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - Q.kpo_shortcut_debt * 3 -
    Q.kpo_funds_delayed - kpoFinalDualism * 0.06;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 0;
if (kpoFinalScore >= 70) {
    Q.kpo_final_status = "Green — final payment file credible";
    Q.kpo_funds_available += 4;
    Q.kpo_funds_status = "Final file credible; completion audit pending";
    Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 4;
    Q.kpo_last_summary = "A strong delivery record releases the last substantial tranche.";
    Q.news_headline = "The final KPO file enters the green lane";
} else if (kpoFinalScore >= 32) {
    Q.kpo_final_status = "Amber — corrective completion required";
    Q.kpo_funds_available += 2;
    Q.kpo_funds_delayed += 1;
    Q.kpo_funds_status = "Partial release; corrective completion required";
    Q.kpo_last_funds_change = 2;
    Q.kpo_last_summary = "Part of the final file clears while weak projects enter correction.";
    Q.news_headline = "The final KPO file receives a partial green light";
} else {
    Q.kpo_final_status = "Red — final payment at risk";
    Q.kpo_funds_delayed += 4;
    Q.kpo_funds_status = "Final payment at risk";
    Q.fiscal_stress += 5;
    Q.kpo_last_summary = "Missed delivery and shortcut debt threaten the final payment.";
    Q.news_headline = "The final KPO file enters a funding crisis";
}
const kpoNames26b = {
    ko: "KO",
    p2050: "Poland 2050",
    psl: "PSL",
    pis: "PiS",
    konf: "Konfederacja"
};
const kpoSeats26b = function(code) {
    return Q["ministry_" + code + "_in_cabinet"]
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q[code + "_seats"]) || 0)
        : 0;
};
Q.kpo_partner_code = Object.keys(kpoNames26b)
    .filter(function(code) { return kpoSeats26b(code) > 0; })
    .sort(function(first, second) {
        return (second == Q.government_party ? 1e6 : kpoSeats26b(second)) -
            (first == Q.government_party ? 1e6 : kpoSeats26b(first));
    })[0] || "";
Q.kpo_partner_name =
    kpoNames26b[Q.kpo_partner_code] || "the coalition's other parties";
Q.kpo_partner_leader =
    String(Q[Q.kpo_partner_code + "_leader"] || "").trim() ||
    String(Q.prime_minister || "the senior partner");
Q.kpo_ledger_public = Q.kpo_ledger_public ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_prior_ledger = Q.kpo_ledger_public;
Q.kpo_opposition_file = Q.kpo_opposition_file ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_owner = String(Q.kpo_owner || "none");
Q.kpo_prior_owner = Q.kpo_owner;
Q.kpo_grudge_active = Q.kpo_grudge_active ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_grudge_name = String(Q.kpo_grudge_name || "");
Q.kpo_grudge_leader = String(Q.kpo_grudge_leader || "");
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = String(Q.kpo_grudge_reason || "");
Q.kpo_uncommitted = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.kpo_funds_available - Q.kpo_funds_spent
);
!}

= July 2026 — The final deadline

Final status: **[+ kpo_final_status +]**. Uncommitted blocks:
**[+ kpo_uncommitted +]**.

Six weeks. On 31 August the programme ends — not the spending, the eligibility.
A project that is ninety per cent complete on 1 September is not a project
running slightly late; it is a hole in the ground with an invoice nobody in
Europe is obliged to pay.

[? if pip_final_retry_resolved: PIP follow-up: **[+ pip_final_retry_status +]**.?]

[? if kpo_final_status = "Green — final payment file credible": The file is credible and the room knows it. Two and a half years of unglamorous decisions — corrections nobody cheered, ledgers nobody wanted to sign, permitting officers hired instead of ribbons cut — have bought the one thing that cannot be improvised in six weeks: a genuine choice about what to finish.?]
[? if kpo_final_status = "Amber — corrective completion required": The file can still be rescued, but only by somebody standing up in this room and saying which projects are being abandoned. Everybody understands this. Nobody has yet said a project's name out loud, because every project has a mayor and most mayors have a party.?]
[? if kpo_final_status = "Red — final payment at risk": The fund is now a fiscal crisis with a date on it, and the meeting is not about completion any more. It is about the sentence each party intends to use in the autumn, and **[+ kpo_partner_leader +]** has clearly written theirs already.?]

[? if kpo_owner = "lewica": Every one of those decisions has our name attached, because we spent two years making sure it would. There is no version of August in which this is somebody else's programme.?]
[? if kpo_owner = "chancellery": The programme belongs to **[+ prime_minister +]** in the public record, which means the failures do too — and so, awkwardly, do the parts we built.?]
[? if kpo_owner = "shared": The scoreboard has every party's column on it, which was the point, and which now means no single party can be blamed and no single party can claim it. In an election year that is a defensive weapon and nothing else.?]

- @final_ready_work
- @final_independent_audit
- @final_paper_close
- @final_opposition_rescue
- @final_opposition_blame

@final_ready_work
title: Protect ready social projects and abandon prestige schemes
subtitle: Names the schemes that will not be finished, six weeks out, in front of the ministers who own them.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: kpo_uncommitted >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: No released tranche remains to redirect.
on-arrival: {!
const finalCommit = Math.min(3, Q.kpo_uncommitted);
Q.kpo_funds_spent += finalCommit;
Q.kpo_delivery += 6;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 4);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 5;
Q.government_delivery += 4;
Q.local_network += 3;
Q.ko_relation -= 2;
Q.kpo_owner = "lewica";
Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "Lewica chose what would finish and named what would not";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change += 5;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 6;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The coalition sacrifices prestige projects to finish work people can use.";
Q.news_headline = "The final KPO block moves to projects that can open on time";
!}

The prestige schemes are abandoned so that everything with a realistic
completion date can be finished properly rather than everything being finished
badly. The list of the abandoned is read out. Some of them are handsome, some
are well advanced, and every one of them belongs to a minister who is in the
room and will not forget being in it.

[? if kpo_grudge_active: **[+ kpo_grudge_leader +]** loses two schemes and leaves without speaking. It is the second time; the first was [+ kpo_grudge_reason +], and there will not be a third opportunity for us to need anything from [+ kpo_grudge_name +] before the campaign.?]

What is completed by 31 August is smaller than what was announced in 2022, and
it exists. A finished clinic outranks a rendered proposal in every accounting
that matters, and the people who eventually use it will never know there was an
argument about it in July.

- @kpo_result: Finish what can finish

@final_independent_audit
title: Accept a smaller claim and submit an independent completion audit
subtitle: [? if kpo_ledger_public = 1: The ledger and the protocol already say what was due; auditors we do not control confirm the rest.?][? if kpo_ledger_public = 0: Claim less than we could and hand the verification to auditors we do not control.?]
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
// A programme that has been publishing its own dates for two years can be
// audited in six weeks; one that has not is reconstructing its own history.
const auditHasRecord = Q.kpo_ledger_public ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_milestones += auditHasRecord ? 3 : 2;
Q.kpo_delivery += 3;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.kpo_shortcut_debt - (auditHasRecord ? 6 : 4)
);
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.kpo_deadline_pressure - 2);
Q.kpo_public_credit += 2;
Q.public_trust += auditHasRecord ? 5 : 3;
Q.ko_relation -= 2;
Q.kpo_owner = "shared";
Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "The final file is smaller than it could be and was verified by somebody else";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change += 2;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 3;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "A smaller honest file loses money but protects trust and later audits.";
Q.news_headline = "The government submits a smaller independently audited KPO file";
!}

We claim less than we could and hand the verification to auditors we do not
appoint, do not brief and cannot telephone. Money that could have been argued
for — and might even have been won — is left on the table in front of
**[+ finance_minister +]**, who says so, twice, for the record.

[? if kpo_ledger_public = 1: The audit takes six weeks because the record already exists. Two years of published dates mean the auditors are checking a story rather than assembling one, and three ministries discover that the ledger they resented in 2024 is the only reason their own work can be certified at all.?]
[? if kpo_ledger_public = 0: The audit takes six weeks that we do not comfortably have, because before anything can be verified it has to be reconstructed: what was promised, by whom, and when. Half of that reconstruction is a matter of somebody's recollection.?]

What the smaller claim buys is the single thing a recovery programme cannot
recover once it is gone: a file that later scrutiny confirms instead of
unpicking. The Commission notices immediately. The next government notices in
about three years, when it goes looking for something to prosecute and finds
paperwork instead.

- @kpo_result: Submit the honest file

@final_paper_close
title: Certify every arguable milestone and fight over it later
subtitle: [? if kpo_ledger_public = 1: Meet the date by certifying lines whose slipped dates we published ourselves.?][? if kpo_ledger_public = 0: Meet the filing date and hand the crisis to auditors, lawyers and the next government.?]
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
// Certifying contested lines is worse where the coalition published its own
// dates: the contradiction is a document, not an allegation.
const closeAgainstRecord = Q.kpo_ledger_public ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_milestones += 6;
Q.kpo_delivery -= 4;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt += closeAgainstRecord ? 9 : 7;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure -= 1;
Q.kpo_public_credit -= closeAgainstRecord ? 7 : 5;
Q.public_trust -= closeAgainstRecord ? 6 : 4;
Q.razem_dissent += 7;
Q.kpo_owner_label =
    "The file was certified complete and the argument was postponed";
Q.kpo_last_credit_change -= closeAgainstRecord ? 7 : 5;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = -4;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The filing deadline is met by transferring the crisis to audits and courts.";
Q.news_headline = "The coalition certifies a contested final KPO file";
!}

Every arguable milestone is certified and the deadline is met. The claim goes in
complete, on time, and containing eleven statements that somebody will have to
defend in front of somebody else. The officials who drafted them ask, in
writing, to have the instruction confirmed in writing. It is.

[? if kpo_ledger_public = 1: The problem is our own paper. Six of the certified lines are lines whose slipped dates we published ourselves, under our own party's column, and the contradiction is therefore not an allegation anybody has to prove — it is two documents, both signed by this coalition, in the same public archive.?]
[? if kpo_ledger_public = 0: Nothing published contradicts it, which is the entire reason this is survivable. What is coming instead is the audit, and audits do not run on news cycles.?]

The defending will be done by auditors, by lawyers, and by whoever is holding
the ministry in two years' time. We have converted a delivery problem into a
legal one, which is slower, much quieter, and — with an election first —
somebody else's.

- @kpo_result: Certify and defend later

@final_opposition_rescue
title: Support a narrow completion act for workers and municipalities
subtitle: Save the projects in the annex and hand [+ prime_minister +] a majority nine months before an election.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_milestones += 2;
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 3;
Q.kpo_public_credit += 3;
Q.ko_relation += 3;
Q.psl_relation += 2;
Q.local_network += 2;
Q.labor_credibility += 2;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change += 3;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The Left supplies passage votes for useful projects without claiming to implement them from opposition.";
Q.news_headline = "Opposition votes rescue the final social KPO projects";
!}

We supply the votes for the completion act because the municipal works and the
labour projects are inside it, and because a bus depot in Podlaskie does not
become less necessary when the government building it is one we intend to
replace.

**[+ prime_minister +]** gets the majority and keeps every part of the delivery
that was always going to be kept, and the press notice at Friday's briefing
makes no mention of where the votes came from.

Our own side asks, reasonably and loudly, why we rescued a cabinet that will
spend the spring campaigning against us. The answer is the annex — a list of
sixty-one projects that will now open. It is an extremely poor slogan and a
completely real one.

- @kpo_result: Pass the narrow act

@final_opposition_blame
title: Publish the missed-project map and refuse emergency cover
subtitle: Every exposed project, dated and attributed. Some of them will now not be built.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_public_credit += 5;
Q.media_capacity += 4;
Q.ko_relation -= 6;
Q.psl_relation -= 3;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure += 3;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.kpo_last_credit_change += 5;
Q.kpo_last_delivery_change = 0;
Q.kpo_last_summary = "The map wins clear opposition credit while leaving weak projects exposed.";
Q.news_headline = "The Left maps every project endangered by the KPO deadline";
!}

The map goes out with every exposed project marked, dated and attributed to the
ministry answerable for it. No emergency cover, no rescue votes, no shared
ownership of a failure that was not ours to cause. It is published on a Monday
and leads three bulletins by Tuesday.

[? if kpo_opposition_file = 1: The map is only possible because somebody has been keeping the underlying list since 2024. Nothing about it can be dismissed as a campaign document, because it is the same document it was two years ago with the dates moved on.?]
[? if kpo_opposition_file = 0: Assembled in nineteen days from public registers, it is accurate and obviously new, and the ministry's first response is to ask why we have only noticed now.?]

It is the clearest political position available to an opposition in July 2026
and it costs something that can be counted. Several of the projects on that map
will now not be finished, partly because we refused to help finish them, and the
towns concerned can read their own names on it in the same colour as everybody
else's.

- @kpo_result: Publish the map


@kpo_result
title: The KPO ledger moves
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.kpo_funds_available =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_available))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_funds_available))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_funds_spent =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_spent))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_funds_spent))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_delivery =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_delivery))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_delivery))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_milestones =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_milestones))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_milestones))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_public_credit =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_public_credit))
        ? Number(Q.kpo_public_credit)
        : 0;
Q.kpo_deadline_pressure =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_deadline_pressure))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_deadline_pressure))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_shortcut_debt =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_shortcut_debt))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_shortcut_debt))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_funds_delayed =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.kpo_funds_delayed))
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.kpo_funds_delayed))
        : 0;
Q.kpo_uncommitted = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.kpo_funds_available - Q.kpo_funds_spent
);
Q.kpo_progress_band =
    Q.kpo_delivery >= 24
        ? "Delivery visible"
        : (Q.kpo_delivery >= 12
            ? "Delivery partial"
            : "Delivery fragile");
Q.kpo_owner = String(Q.kpo_owner || "none");
Q.kpo_owner_label = String(Q.kpo_owner_label || "").trim() ||
    "No party has attached itself to the file";
Q.kpo_grudge_active = Q.kpo_grudge_active ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpo_grudge_name = String(Q.kpo_grudge_name || "");
Q.kpo_grudge_leader = String(Q.kpo_grudge_leader || "");
Q.kpo_grudge_reason = String(Q.kpo_grudge_reason || "");
if (!Q.kpo_grudge_name || !Q.kpo_grudge_reason) Q.kpo_grudge_active = 0;
!}

= The file moves

[+ kpo_last_summary +]

[? if kpo_delivery >= 24: In the counties, the fund has stopped being a word
from the news. There are sites with hoardings, contractors with signed dates
and clinics that have taken delivery of something. A programme people can walk
past is harder for any future minister to describe as somebody's abstraction.?]
[? if kpo_delivery >= 12 and kpo_delivery < 24: Enough has been signed to point
at, and not enough to answer the obvious question. Half the mayors on the list
have a start date; the other half have a letter explaining why theirs is
delayed, and every one of those letters is a small deposit of future anger.?]
[? if kpo_delivery < 12: On paper the plan is alive. On the ground almost
nothing has broken earth, and the people who were told to prepare bids are
beginning to treat the whole exercise as a Warsaw hobby.?]

[? if kpo_deadline_pressure >= 12: The 2026 completion date has stopped being a
horizon and become a problem. Every project office knows that work which cannot
finish cannot be certified, and that uncertified work is money returned.?]

Ownership on the file tonight: **[+ kpo_owner_label +]**.

[? if kpo_last_credit_change >= 4: **Our imprint is unmistakable.** Voters can name what Lewica forced, and our partners can no longer fold it into a generic government success.?]
[? if kpo_last_credit_change >= 1 and kpo_last_credit_change < 4: **We have a claim, not ownership.** Our work is visible, but coalition partners remain in the photograph and will contest the authorship.?]
[? if kpo_last_credit_change = 0: **The ledger moves without us.** The result is administrative or belongs to the institution that acted.?]
[? if kpo_last_credit_change < 0: **We lose the story.** Work may continue, but another party owns it or our factions inherit the blame.?]

[? if kpo_grudge_active: [+ kpo_grudge_name +] is carrying an unpaid account for [+ kpo_grudge_reason +], and **[+ kpo_grudge_leader +]** will choose when to present it. It will not be a month in which we can afford it.?]

[? if kpo_last_delivery_change >= 4: People, contracts and projects now move;
the advance is large enough to survive the press conference.?]
[? if kpo_last_delivery_change >= 1 and kpo_last_delivery_change < 4:
Some implementation advances, but the next review can still expose what the
coalition left unfinished.?]
[? if kpo_last_delivery_change = 0: We changed scrutiny or ownership, not what
the state can deliver.?]
[? if kpo_last_delivery_change < 0: The paper file improved by displacing work
that people could have used.?]

[? if kpo_last_funds_change > 0: A further tranche has been released, still
subject to completion and audit.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Continue
